{
  "id": "pc-sequences",
  "chapterNumber": "8",
  "title": {
    "en": "Sequences & Series",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A <em>sequence</em> is an ordered list of numbers; a <em>series</em> is the sum of a sequence's terms. Arithmetic and geometric types appear in financial models, while infinite series connect to calculus through limits.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Arithmetic sequences & series",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Common difference \\(d\\); \\(n\\)-th term and sum:</p>\\[a_n=a_1+(n-1)d,\\quad S_n=\\frac{n}{2}(a_1+a_n)=\\frac{n}{2}[2a_1+(n-1)d].\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Geometric sequences & series",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Common ratio \\(r\\); \\(n\\)-th term, finite sum, and infinite sum:</p>\\[a_n=a_1\\,r^{n-1},\\quad S_n=\\frac{a_1(1-r^n)}{1-r}\\;(r\\neq1),\\quad S_\\infty=\\frac{a_1}{1-r}\\;(|r|&lt;1).\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Geometric partial sums",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "pcGeoCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "Dots at the partial sums S1 through Sn of a geometric series, with a dashed line at the infinite sum when the absolute value of r is less than 1.",
          "ar": null
